    "content": "A delegation from the Pakistan Air Force arrived in Mogadishu on September 19, 2026, for an official visit aimed at bolstering military cooperation between Pakistan and Somalia. The delegation was led by Air Marshal Muhammad Sarfraz, Deputy Chief of Air Staff of the Pakistan Air Force, and was received by Brigadier General Abdirahman Mahmud Haji, Commander of the Somali Air Force.\n\nThe visit is part of ongoing efforts to strengthen ties between the two countries' air forces. During their stay, the officials are expected to discuss areas of mutual interest, including training, capacity building, and technical support. The Somali Air Force has been rebuilding its capabilities after decades of conflict, and partnerships with foreign militaries are seen as crucial to that process.\n\nPakistan has historically maintained friendly relations with Somalia, providing support in various sectors, including defense and education. This latest engagement follows a series of diplomatic and security exchanges between the two nations. In recent years, Somalia has sought to enhance its military ties with several countries to counter persistent security threats, particularly from al-Shabab.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this visit signals continued international interest in stabilizing Somalia and strengthening its institutions. Many diaspora members have supported peacebuilding and development efforts, and improved security cooperation can contribute to a more stable environment for investment and return. The diaspora often closely follows such developments as indicators of progress in the homeland.\n\nThe delegation's visit is expected to conclude with agreements on further collaboration, though specific details have not been publicly disclosed. The Somali government has not yet issued a detailed statement on the outcomes of the talks. The visit underscores the growing role of Pakistan as a partner in Somalia's security sector reform.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/19/wafdi-sare-oo-ka-socda-ciidanka-cirka-pakistan-oo-muqdisho-soo-gaaray/",
