    "summary": "Turkish government rejects social media claims of visa restrictions on Somali citizens, calling them baseless.",
    "content": "The Turkish government has denied reports circulating on social media and some media outlets that it has imposed visa restrictions on Somali citizens. In an official statement, Turkish authorities described the claims as unfounded and reiterated that no such measures are in place.\n\nThe rumors had spread rapidly online, causing concern among Somali communities both in Turkey and abroad. Many Somalis travel to Turkey for business, education, and medical treatment, making any potential visa changes a significant issue.\n\nTurkey has maintained strong ties with Somalia for over a decade, providing humanitarian aid, infrastructure development, and scholarships to Somali students. The two countries have deep economic and diplomatic relations, and Turkey remains a popular destination for Somali travelers.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this denial is reassuring. Many rely on Turkey as a transit point or destination for family visits, trade, and medical care. The false reports had sparked worries about potential disruptions to these activities.\n\nTurkish officials urged the public to rely on official sources for accurate information and warned against spreading unverified news. They emphasized that Turkey continues to welcome Somali citizens under existing visa regulations.\n\nThis incident highlights the importance of verifying information before sharing it, especially on social media platforms where misinformation can spread quickly. The Somali diaspora is encouraged to stay informed through reliable channels.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/turkiga-oo-beeniyay-in-soomaaliya-xayiraad-fiiso-saartay-muwaadiniinteeda-dalkaasi/425791/",
