    "slug": "somalia-and-eu-discuss-strengthening-cooperation",
    "summary": "Somalia's Deputy Foreign Minister received credentials from the new EU Ambassador to Somalia, Laszlo Mathe, and discussed ongoing EU support for Somalia's sovereignty and unity.",
    "content": "Mogadishu, September 19, 2026 — Somalia's Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Hassan Mohamed Ali (Nadara), today accepted the credentials of the new European Union Ambassador to Somalia, Laszlo Mathe. The meeting also marked the formal recall of the previous EU Ambassador to Somalia.\n\nThe Deputy Minister expressed gratitude for the European Union's consistent support to the Federal Government of Somalia, particularly its backing for Somalia's independence, unity, and territorial integrity. The two sides discussed ways to enhance bilateral cooperation across various sectors.\n\nThis diplomatic engagement comes as Somalia continues to navigate complex regional dynamics and internal challenges, including security operations against militant groups and efforts to complete its constitutional review process. The European Union has been a key partner in providing development aid, humanitarian assistance, and capacity-building support to Somali institutions.\n\nThe new EU Ambassador, Laszlo Mathe, is expected to build on the work of his predecessor in deepening ties between Brussels and Mogadishu. His appointment signals the EU's continued commitment to supporting stability and development in the Horn of Africa nation.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this meeting underscores the importance of international partnerships in fostering peace and prosperity back home. Many diaspora members are actively involved in Somalia's reconstruction and rely on stable diplomatic relations to facilitate investments, remittances, and family reunification.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/19/soomaaliya-iyo-midowga-yurub-oo-ka-wada-hadlay-xoojinta-iskaashiga-labada-dhinac/",
